{"name":"Sky Dancer","hex":"#4499ff","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"},{"term":"dancer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who dances, usually as a hobby, an occupation, or a profession.","A stripper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dancer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sky Dancers","blocks":[{"text":"Sky Dancers are a line of toys manufactured by Galoob which were popular in the mid-1990s and were the basis for an animated series. The toys consisted of a pullstring base and a doll with foam wings. When the doll was inserted into the base and the string was pulled, it would launch into the air and spin its wings like a propeller as it flew, similar to a helicopter."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_Dancers","wikidata":"Q3828812"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance","wikidata":"Q11639"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/500px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/1280px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg/500px-Sky_over_Munich_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cirriform clouds and a quarter Moon in the blue daytime sky over Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASky_over_Munich_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg/500px-Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg/1280px-Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg/500px-Blue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sky during day time","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Sky%2C_Dhaka%2C_Bangladesh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Clear_skies_over_Yekaterinburg.jpg/500px-Clear_skies_over_Yekaterinburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Clear_skies_over_Yekaterinburg.jpg/1280px-Clear_skies_over_Yekaterinburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Clear_skies_over_Yekaterinburg.jpg/500px-Clear_skies_over_Yekaterinburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clear skies over Yekaterinburg, Russia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClear_skies_over_Yekaterinburg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Rayleigh_sunlight_scattering.png/500px-Rayleigh_sunlight_scattering.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Rayleigh_sunlight_scattering.png/500px-Rayleigh_sunlight_scattering.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Earth's atmosphere scatters a greater proportion of blue light than of red light.","link":"https:/